// The second file named 'same', which is what ErrorDupFile reports. A module's
// files are named by their basenames -- to 'include', and to every diagnostic
// reported against one -- so two of them sharing a name leave neither nameable.
//
// It is not parsed at all: a file that cannot join the module is dropped rather
// than read, so nothing in here is a declaration of anything.

fn threeOnly() i64 {
  3i64;
}
